./docs/quests/2026-11-15-pi-engine-conductor/QUEST.md:38:| desk | a `bp3 worktree` checkout; two levels: a **quest desk** at `.bp3/desks/<quest>/conductor` (the conductor's cwd for a whole `/induct-quest` drive) and **run desks** at `.bp3/desks/<quest>/<exp>/<run_id>` (one child Run's cwd). Nesting is what makes parallel quest execution structural: one conductor per quest desk, one child per run desk, no shared checkout at either level |
