./docs/quests/2026-11-15-pi-engine-conductor/QUEST.md:281:| Desks nest (owner, red-ink round 4 amendment) | two levels matching the two merge stages: a **quest desk** (one per `/induct-quest`, the conductor's cwd for the whole drive, keyed by quest) and **run desks** inside it (keyed by run-id, prepared by the pi extension at spawn). `land` merges exp→quest inside the quest desk's world; the main tree sees the quest branch only at `quest_fin`. The conductor never conducts from the owner's main tree — the no-human drive's self-inflicted `E_DIRTY_TREE` park is the scar this prevents. Quest desk releases last, after its run desks, with the same dirty refusal. Paths: derivation today is `.bp3/worktrees/<quest>/<exp>/<run_id>` (worktree.ml); after Exp 1.2 renames worktree → desk in code, run desks live at `.bp3/desks/<quest>/<exp>/<run_id>` and the quest desk takes the reserved slot `.bp3/desks/<quest>/conductor` in the same namespace. **Purpose: parallel quest execution** — two `/induct-quest` conductors, two quest desks, no shared checkout at either level; the cli-small-fixes line of work (its `test/worktree.sh` desk cases) is the proving ground this convention inherits |
